      <section id="overview" class="doc-section active" aria-labelledby="overview-heading">
        <h2 id="overview-heading">Overview</h2>
        <p>Boing Network is an independent Layer 1 built from first principles, where quality is enforced by the protocol. It is independent of other chains and designed for sustainable value, uncapped supply with floor-triggered rebalancing, and 100% transparent governance and tokenomics.</p>
        <h3>Pick your path</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>👋 <strong>Everyday users</strong> — Create a wallet at <a href="https://boing.express" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Express</a>, request testnet BOING at <a href="/faucet">the faucet</a>, then look up your account on <a href="https://boing.observer" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Observer</a>. Move liquidity with <a href="https://boing.finance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Finance</a> using Boing Express on Boing L1.</li>
          <li>🛠️ <strong>Developers</strong> — Public RPC <code>https://testnet-rpc.boing.network/</code>. Addresses are 32-byte hex (64 characters), Ed25519 + BLAKE3, not EVM. Start with <a href="#getting-started">Getting Started</a> and <a href="#rpc-api">RPC API</a>. TypeScript: <code>npm install @boing-network/boing-sdk</code> (source under repo <code>boing-sdk/</code>).</li>
          <li>🛰️ <strong>Operators</strong> — Bootnodes, Fly cluster, and the Worker gateway are documented in the repository <code>docs/TESTNET.md</code> and <code>docs/FLY-IO.md</code>. Upgrading a laptop node does not change the public explorer.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>The six pillars</h3>
        <p>In order: <strong>🔐 Security</strong> → <strong>⚡ Scalability</strong> → <strong>🌍 Decentralization</strong> → <strong>🧬 Authenticity</strong> → <strong>🔎 Transparency</strong> → <strong>✅ True quality assurance</strong>. Protocol + product narrative: <a href="/pdfs/BOING-NETWORK-WHITEPAPER.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Whitepaper (PDF)</a>. The written pillars are the <a href="/pdfs/SIX-PILLARS.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">SIX-PILLARS PDF</a> (also on <a href="/about">/about</a>). Plain-language overview: <a href="/pdfs/BOING-NETWORK-ESSENTIALS.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BOING-NETWORK-ESSENTIALS (PDF)</a>. Technical companion: <a href="/pdfs/BOING-NETWORK-TECHNICAL-ESSENTIALS.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BOING-NETWORK-TECHNICAL-ESSENTIALS (PDF)</a>. QA detail: <a href="/pdfs/QUALITY-ASSURANCE-NETWORK.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">QUALITY-ASSURANCE-NETWORK (PDF)</a>.</p>
        <h3>Recent enhancements &amp; optimizations</h3>
        <p>Network-wide improvements include: re-insert of failed txs into mempool, RPC methods <code>boing_qaCheck</code> and QA error codes, <code>boing_getBalance</code> / <code>boing_getAccount</code>, <strong>native DEX discovery</strong> on-chain (<code>boing_listDexPools</code>, <code>boing_listDexTokens</code>, <code>boing_getDexToken</code>; capability names also appear under <code>boing_getNetworkInfo.developer.dex_discovery_methods</code>), unsigned <code>boing_simulateContractCall</code> for calldata dry-runs, six-pillars and essentials documentation, Protocol QA phase in the roadmap. QA pillar enhancements (pre-flight checks, structured errors, public metrics, versioned rule sets, appeal path) are documented in <a href="/pdfs/QUALITY-ASSURANCE-NETWORK.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">QUALITY-ASSURANCE-NETWORK (PDF)</a>. For the full list of implemented and planned enhancements, see <a href="/pdfs/DEVELOPMENT-AND-ENHANCEMENTS.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DEVELOPMENT-AND-ENHANCEMENTS (PDF)</a>.</p>
        <h3>What this documentation covers</h3>
        <p><strong>Getting Started</strong> — Prerequisites, build, run a node (full or validator), first transaction. <strong>Network Overview</strong> — Block time, consensus, key facts. <strong>Tokenomics</strong> — Supply model, fees, staking, waves. <strong>Architecture & Features</strong> — Native AA, adaptive gas, cross-chain, slashing, governance. <strong>RPC API</strong> — All JSON-RPC methods, params, and error codes. <strong>Operations</strong> — CLI, monitoring, troubleshooting, incident response. <strong>Roadmap</strong> — Phased build status. <strong>Testnet</strong> — Join the live testnet (bootnodes, faucet, portal). <strong>Security</strong> — Protocol, network, and operational security. <strong>Governance & Transparency</strong> — How decisions and parameters are visible and verifiable. <strong>Resources</strong> — Links to repo, landing page, and other pages.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="getting-started" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Getting Started</h2>
        <h3>Prerequisites</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Rust</strong> — Latest stable (1.70+). Install via <code>rustup</code>.</li>
          <li><strong>OS</strong> — Linux, macOS, or Windows (WSL recommended on Windows).</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Clone and build</h3>
        <p>From the <a href="https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network" target="_blank" rel="noopener">boing.network</a> repository:</p>
        <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network.git
cd boing.network
cargo build --release</code></pre>
        <h3>Directory layout after build</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>target/release/boing-node</code> — Node binary.</li>
          <li><code>target/release/boing</code> — CLI binary.</li>
          <li><code>~/.boing/</code> or <code>./data/</code> (with <code>--data-dir</code>) — Chain and state data.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Run a node</h3>
        <p><strong>Full node (non-validator):</strong></p>
        <pre><code>cargo run -p boing-node</code></pre>
        <p>RPC is available at <code>http://127.0.0.1:8545</code> by default.</p>
        <p><strong>Validator node:</strong></p>
        <pre><code>cargo run -p boing-node -- --validator --rpc-port 8545</code></pre>
        <p>Produces blocks when there are pending transactions.</p>
        <p><strong>With a custom data directory:</strong></p>
        <pre><code>cargo run -p boing-node -- --data-dir ./boing-data --rpc-port 8545</code></pre>
        <h3>Options</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><code>--validator</code> — Run as a block producer.</li>
          <li><code>--rpc-port &lt;port&gt;</code> — RPC port (default: 8545).</li>
          <li><code>--data-dir &lt;path&gt;</code> — Data directory for chain and state.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>First transaction</h3>
        <p>Use the JSON-RPC API at <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:8545/</code>. See the <a href="#rpc-api">RPC API</a> section for <code>boing_submitTransaction</code>, <code>boing_simulateTransaction</code>, and <code>boing_chainHeight</code>.</p>
        <h3>Next steps</h3>
        <p>See <a href="#operations">Operations</a> for CLI commands, monitoring, and troubleshooting; <a href="#rpc-api">RPC API</a> for all methods; and <a href="#tokenomics">Tokenomics</a> if you plan to run a validator or stake.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="network-overview" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Network Overview</h2>
        <p>Boing is a greenfield L1 — original architecture, not a fork — with no reliance on other chains.</p>
        <h3>Design principles</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Independent</strong> — Your own stack, built from first principles; not a framework clone.</li>
          <li><strong>Independent</strong> — Core protocol does not depend on another L1 for consensus, execution, or identity.</li>
          <li><strong>Decentralized</strong> — Permissionless validators and full nodes.</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent</strong> — 100% openness in design, tokenomics, and governance.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Key parameters</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Block time</strong> — ~2 seconds target when transactions are pending. Blocks are produced only when transactions are present, so a quiet network can sit on the same tip for hours.</li>
          <li><strong>Consensus</strong> — Proof of Stake (PoS) with BFT-style consensus; validators stake BOING.</li>
          <li><strong>State</strong> — Sparse Merkle tree commitments and proofs in current <code>boing-state</code> (see repository technical specification; Verkle remains a documented upgrade path in code comments).</li>
          <li><strong>RPC port</strong> — Default 8545 (HTTP JSON-RPC).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="tokenomics" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Tokenomics</h2>
        <p>Plain-language overview (allocation, fees, quest/bounty pots, testnet ≠ mainnet claim): <a href="/pdfs/BOING-TOKENOMICS-AND-INCENTIVIZED-TESTNET.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BOING-TOKENOMICS-AND-INCENTIVIZED-TESTNET (PDF)</a>. Draft tables with Proposed vs Undecided: <a href="/pdfs/BOING-INITIAL-TOKENOMICS.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">BOING-INITIAL-TOKENOMICS (PDF)</a>. No TGE date is asserted.</p>
        <h3>Supply model</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Locked (BN-155)</strong> — <strong>1 billion BOING</strong> genesis / initial supply (<code>INITIAL_SUPPLY</code>); supply ceiling after genesis is <strong>uncapped</strong> (not a 1B hard cap).</li>
          <li><strong>Decimals</strong> — <strong>18</strong> (1 BOING = 10<sup>18</sup> base units).</li>
          <li><strong>Emissions</strong> — Block rewards continue past 1B under the declining schedule + floor; shipping code does <strong>not</strong> clamp minting at 1B. Code mints ~70% of each block emission to the proposer.</li>
          <li><strong>Design narrative</strong> — Uncapped supply with floor-triggered rebalancing remains the long-form sustainability model in the design plan. No TGE / mainnet calendar date is asserted. Testnet ≠ mainnet claim.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Fee allocation</h3>
        <p><strong>Proposed design target:</strong> <strong>80% validators</strong>, <strong>20% treasury</strong> (burn optional 0%). <strong>Current public testnet runtime:</strong> protocol gas defaults to <strong>100% treasury</strong>; tips and block emission go to the proposer.</p>
        <h3>Initial supply allocation (at launch)</h3>
        <p><strong>Proposed</strong> genesis pie (not final — exact buckets still <strong>Undecided</strong>): <strong>Staking 50%</strong> · <strong>Treasury 20%</strong> · <strong>Community &amp; Grants 15%</strong> · <strong>Team &amp; ops 15%</strong>. Older marketing charts used ~55 / 30 / 15 without a Team line; see <a href="/pdfs/BOING-INITIAL-TOKENOMICS.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">initial tokenomics draft</a>. Staking is topped up by ongoing block emissions (uncapped after the 1B genesis).</p>
        <h3>Floor-triggered waves</h3>
        <p><strong>Genesis</strong> — 1B initial supply. <strong>Ongoing</strong> — Validators and treasury earn from fees; emissions continue uncapped under the declining schedule. <strong>Floor</strong> — When circulating supply reaches the defined floor, the protocol can trigger a rebalance. <strong>New wave</strong> — A new wave of tokens may be minted (size and destination set by protocol/governance) to restore balance. All parameters (floor, wave size, trigger) are intended to be on-chain and transparent.</p>
        <h3>Emission schedule (block rewards)</h3>
        <p><strong>Proposed:</strong> Year 1 ~8% of the 1B base, then decay ≈ 0.85 per year; Year 10+ targets a <strong>1% floor</strong> (or 0% if fees suffice). Formula: <code>emission_year_n = emission_year_1 × (decay)^(n-1)</code>. Shipping mint path credits ~70% of the year-N emission to the round proposer.</p>
        <h3>Staking and validator economics</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Min stake</strong> — Accessible (e.g. 10,000 BOING) for broad participation.</li>
          <li><strong>Staking yield</strong> — 5–15% early, 3–8% at maturity.</li>
          <li><strong>Commission</strong> — Validators typically 5–10%; delegators keep the rest.</li>
          <li><strong>Unbonding</strong> — 14–21 days.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>dApp incentive caps</h3>
        <p>Per-dApp cap per epoch is governance-controlled (e.g. 50,000 BOING/month). Total dApp pool is a share of fees (e.g. 5% of treasury). Prevents one dApp capturing all incentives; overflow goes to treasury.</p>
        <p>Charts and visuals: see the <a href="/#tokenomics">landing page tokenomics</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section id="architecture" class="doc-section">
        <h2>Architecture & Features</h2>
        <p>Boing aims to deliver distinct features as protocol primitives rather than add-on contracts.</p>
        <h3>Core features</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Native Account Abstraction</strong> — Gasless txs, social recovery, session keys built into the protocol (not a contract layer).</li>
          <li><strong>Adaptive Gas Model</strong> — Gas costs adapt to congestion in real time with predictable upper bounds.</li>
          <li><strong>Native Cross-Chain Primitives</strong> — Protocol-level bridges and cross-chain messaging (light clients, not third-party contracts only).</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent Slashing</strong> — Clear, auditable slashing conditions and appeal mechanisms; delegators see why validators were slashed.</li>
          <li><strong>On-Chain Governance with Time Locks</strong> — Parameter changes go through proposal → cooling → execution so the community can react.</li>
        </ul>
        <h3>Additional innovations</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>State rent with grace periods</strong> — Inactive accounts may pay state rent after long grace periods and clear notice.</li>
          <li><strong>Verifiable delay / ordering (VDF)</strong> — Boing-native verifiable delay for fair ordering without depending on another chain.</li>
          <li><strong>Native DeFi primitives</strong> — Protocol-level swap/AMM-style primitives for <a href="https://boing.finance" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Boing Finance</a> integration.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="rpc-api" class="doc-section">
        <h2>RPC API</h2>
        <p>Boing nodes expose <strong>JSON-RPC 2.0</strong> over <strong>HTTP POST</strong> to <code>http://&lt;host&gt;:8545/</code> (default port). The authoritative reference is <a href="https://github.com/Boing-Network/boing.network/blob/main/docs/RPC-API-SPEC.md" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><code>docs/RPC-API-SPEC.md</code></a> in the repository (also <a href="/pdfs/RPC-API-SPEC.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RPC-API-SPEC PDF</a>). Same listener serves <code>GET /live</code>, <code>GET /ready</code>, <code>GET /openapi.json</code>, <code>GET /.well-known/boing-rpc</code>, and <code>GET /ws</code> (newHeads).</p>
        <p>Rate limiting, batch limits, and body size are node-configurable; see the spec and <code>boing_health</code> / <code>boing_getNetworkInfo</code> fields <code>rpc_surface</code> and <code>developer.dex_discovery_methods</code> (stable names for the L1 DEX directory RPC trio).</p>
        <h3>Request format</h3>
        <pre><code>{jsonRpcExample}</code></pre>
        <h3>Response format</h3>
        <p><strong>Success:</strong> <code>{responseSuccessExample}</code>. <strong>Error:</strong> <code>{responseErrorExample}</code>.</p>
        <h3>Methods (current <code>boing-node</code>)</h3>
        <p>Below matches <code>boing_rpcSupportedMethods</code> / <code>crates/boing-node/src/rpc.rs</code>. Params are JSON arrays; 32-byte ids use <code>0x</code> + 64 hex chars unless noted.</p>
        <table class="doc-table rpc-method-table">
          <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Params (summary)</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td><code>boing_chainHeight</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Committed tip height (u64).</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>boing_clientVersion</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>e.g. <code>boing-node/0.1.0</code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>boing_rpcSupportedMethods</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Sorted list of <code>boing_*</code> names.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>boing_health</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Liveness, <code>head_height</code>, optional <code>chain_id</code>, <code>rpc_surface</code>, <code>rpc_metrics</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>boing_getSyncState</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td><code>head_height</code>, <code>finalized_height</code>, <code>latest_block_hash</code>.</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>boing_getNetworkInfo</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Chain metadata, <code>chain_native</code>, <code>developer</code>, <code>end_user</code>, <code>rpc.not_available</code>, …</td></tr>
            <tr><td><code>boing_getRpcMethodCatalog</code></td><td><code>[]</code></td><td>Embedded catalog for tooling.</td></tr>
